 "elements": {
  "description": [
   {
    "value": "[Clemens, Samuel Langhorne] (b Florida, MO, Nov 30, 1835; d Redding, CT, April 21, 1910). American writer. An examination of his musical interests and opinions reveals two identities – the uncultivated frontiersman who often delighted in satirizing serious music, and the urbane sophisticate who spent many years abroad enjoying it. In A Tramp Abroad (Hartford, CT, 1880) he included humorous impressions (and, in some of the early editions, illustrations) of German operas, chiefly those of Wagner. ",
